---
layout: ent-layout.njk
permalink: /grow-with-us/
pageTitle: "Grow with Us · OpenShore for Enterprise"
pageDescription: "Why OpenShore exists: our mission, the principles we build by, and the founder behind it."
---
{#- Grow with Us (founder, 2026-11-16): the mission, the principles from the
    business plan's appendix, then the founder. The words live in
    src/_data/growWithUs.js; an empty section is left off the page. -#}
{%- set g = growWithUs -%}
      <section class="ent-sec ent-sec--first" aria-labelledby="mission-h">
        <h1 class="ent-eyebrow" id="mission-h">Our mission</h1>
        <p class="ent-statement">{{ g.mission }}</p>
        <p class="ent-body">{{ g.missionLine }}</p>
      </section>

      {#- Why we build it (founder, 2026-11-16): two charts from his consulting
          work, redrawn for the site with no client named. The first is
          Greiner's phases of growth (HBR); the second is illustrative and
          says so. -#}
      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="why-h">
        <h2 class="ent-eyebrow" id="why-h">Why we build it</h2>
        <h3 class="ent-h">Every startup reaches the same scaling points. We build for them.</h3>
        <div class="ent-charts">
          <figure class="ent-chart">
            <figcaption class="ent-chart-title">The scaling points are predictable</figcaption>
            <div class="ent-chart-frame">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 640 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="c1-t c1-d">
                <title id="c1-t">Phases of growth</title>
                <desc id="c1-d">A company grows through three phases, creativity, direction and delegation. Growth breaks at a crisis of leadership between the first two and a crisis of autonomy between the last two. A marker on the first crisis reads: where we come in.</desc>
                <line class="c-guide" x1="270" y1="36" x2="270" y2="272" />
                <line class="c-guide" x1="456" y1="36" x2="456" y2="272" />
                <line class="c-axis" x1="30" y1="274" x2="620" y2="274" />
                <path class="c-line" d="M44 256 Q170 244 254 194 L266 214 L279 178 L292 189 L442 124 L452 144 L464 110 L476 120 L612 58" />
                <text class="c-crisis" x="274" y="124" text-anchor="middle">crisis of leadership</text>
                <text class="c-note" x="456" y="94" text-anchor="middle">crisis of autonomy</text>
                <line class="c-leader" x1="190" y1="176" x2="242" y2="190" />
                <text class="c-mark" x="186" y="172" text-anchor="end">Where we come in</text>
                <circle class="c-halo" cx="254" cy="194" r="13" />
                <circle class="c-dot" cx="254" cy="194" r="6" />
                <text class="c-phase" x="150" y="302" text-anchor="middle">CREATIVITY</text>
                <text class="c-phase" x="363" y="302" text-anchor="middle">DIRECTION</text>
                <text class="c-phase" x="540" y="302" text-anchor="middle">DELEGATION</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <p class="ent-body">Growth arrives in phases, and each phase ends in a predictable crisis. Age runs left to right, company size runs up. The first crisis is leadership: the founder-led phase ends when the founders become the constraint. The way through is direction, where management structure, systems and standards go in, and delegation follows once those standards exist. That first crisis is where the startups we build for are, and it is where OpenShore comes in.</p>
          </figure>
          <figure class="ent-chart">
            <figcaption class="ent-chart-title">Waiting costs more every month <span class="ent-tag">Illustrative</span></figcaption>
            <div class="ent-chart-frame">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 640 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="c2-t c2-d">
                <title id="c2-t">The cost of building nothing</title>
                <desc id="c2-d">As the business grows, its commitments curve steeply upward while the founders' capacity stays nearly flat. The widening gap between them holds fire drills, deciding blind and missed deals.</desc>
                <path class="c-wedge" d="M50 252 C250 222 420 162 590 66 L590 206 C400 214 200 226 50 252 Z" />
                <line class="c-guide" x1="214" y1="56" x2="214" y2="272" />
                <text class="c-phase" x="214" y="46" text-anchor="middle">TODAY</text>
                <line class="c-axis" x1="40" y1="274" x2="600" y2="274" />
                <path class="c-line c-line--sea" d="M50 252 C250 222 420 162 590 66" />
                <path class="c-line" d="M50 252 C200 226 400 214 590 206" />
                <text class="c-label" x="590" y="52" text-anchor="end">commitments</text>
                <text class="c-label" x="590" y="232" text-anchor="end">founder capacity</text>
                <text class="c-wedge-text" x="480" y="156" text-anchor="middle">fire drills</text>
                <text class="c-wedge-text" x="480" y="174" text-anchor="middle">deciding blind</text>
                <text class="c-wedge-text" x="480" y="192" text-anchor="middle">missed deals</text>
                <text class="c-phase" x="320" y="302" text-anchor="middle">AS THE BUSINESS GROWS &#8594;</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <p class="ent-body">Every new customer adds commitments, while what a founding team can carry stays roughly flat. The wedge between those lines is where the fire drills, the blind decisions and the missed deals live, and it widens on its own.</p>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <p class="ent-statement ent-why-close">That gap is why we build OpenShore. It puts the direction layer in early, with expert AI workers beside the team, so founders spend their energy on customers instead of on the gap.</p>
        <p class="ent-source">Source: Larry E. Greiner, “Evolution and Revolution as Organizations Grow,” <i>Harvard Business Review</i> (1972, reissued 1998). The second chart is illustrative, not measured.</p>
      </section>
{% if g.principles.length %}
      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="principles-h">
        <h2 class="ent-eyebrow" id="principles-h">{{ g.principlesTitle }}</h2>
        <p class="ent-body ent-principles-lede">{{ g.principlesLede }}</p>
        <ol class="ent-principles">
{%- for p in g.principles %}
          <li>
            <h3>{{ p.title }}</h3>
            <p>{{ p.body }}</p>
            <p class="ent-decides"><b>Decides</b> {{ p.decides }}</p>
          </li>
{%- endfor %}
        </ol>
      </section>
{% endif %}
{%- if g.founder.paragraphs.length %}
      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="founder-h">
        <h2 class="ent-eyebrow" id="founder-h">The founder</h2>
        <div class="ent-founder">
          {% if g.founder.photo %}<img class="ent-founder-photo" src="/enterprise/founder.jpg?v={{ rev.entFounder }}" alt="{{ g.founder.alt }}" width="640" height="640" />{% endif %}
          <div class="ent-founder-text">
            <h3 class="ent-h">{{ g.founder.name }}</h3>
            <p class="ent-founder-role">{{ g.founder.role }}</p>
{%- for para in g.founder.paragraphs %}
            <p class="ent-body">{{ para }}</p>
{%- endfor %}
            {% if g.founder.linkedin %}<p class="ent-founder-links"><a href="{{ g.founder.linkedin }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a></p>{% endif %}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
{% endif %}
      <section class="ent-cta" aria-labelledby="cta-h">
        <p class="ent-badge"><span class="ent-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Coming in 2027</p>
        <h2 id="cta-h">Build the future of your business with us.</h2>
        <p class="ent-lede">Now onboarding design partners. If you’re interested, email <a href="mailto:{{ site.enterpriseContact }}?subject={{ 'OpenShore for Enterprise design partner' | urlencode }}">{{ site.enterpriseContact }}</a>.</p>
      </section>
